::heading level=1 id=index
bin — project index
::end

::paragraph id=index-lead
**Helpers** is agent-agnostic AI-coding-tool tooling: a single native Rust binary shipping a CLI (`helpers`) and an MCP server, agent-agnostic across Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, and any MCP-capable client. Its `native/` crate also builds **the AI linter** — a linter whose rules are learned from a language's own documentation rather than hand-written. Full documentation for both now lives in dx: `helpers.dx` (the CLI/MCP tool) and `native/index.dx` (the AI linter), linked from the area sections below. `AGENTS.md` and `README.md` stay as trimmed, convention-locked entry points that point here.
::end

::paragraph id=index-purpose
Scaffold from the file tree, written by `dx index`. Improve it: replace each TODO with what the area does and how it connects to the rest, and add `::code src=` blocks for the load-bearing files — they render as the file's current text, never a stale copy. Files below are ranked by how load-bearing they look (entry points, how many files reference them, size); trust the ranking as a place to start, not as the truth. Keep this document true as the code changes.
::end

::heading level=2 id=now
Now
::end

::paragraph id=now-note
The working section — the designated first read of every turn, and its last write. The worklist below is the task's program counter (found / fixing / verified), which makes the task the unit of work instead of the session: it survives compaction, crashes, and handoffs, and a second agent can pick up an unclaimed line. Thoughts land here the moment they form (`dx_append`, `dx_check`) and are promoted into the sections below when they harden. Keep it small — everything else in this document is the archive.
::end

::checklist id=now-worklist
[x] Improve this index: replace each TODO with what the area does
[x] Expose the one-bit/hypervector model core (train + infer) as a reusable library API so bonsai-buddy can train a plant-care head on it (point at native/src/lint_sign.rs, hv_batch.rs, examples/*_train.rs)
[x] Document the model shape in helpers.dx with complete specs for training and inference
[x] Wire the helpers lint report intake (.helpers/lint-feedback.jsonl, scripts/lint-index-*.sh) into a worked errors.dx queue for SARA
[x] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [defaults] Smoke test: verify every helpers MCP tool answers correctly and quickly
[x] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [defaults] Add comprehensive README.md with usage examples and project overview
[x] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [defaults] Add LICENSE file to establish legal terms
[x] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [defaults] Create .gitignore to exclude node_modules, build artifacts, and environment files
[x] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [defaults] Set up CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions or similar) to run tests on every commit
[ ] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [cap: cap-full-build] Build release binary via 'cargo build --release --bins' in native/ directory after Rust toolchain is configured; verify cap-full-build gate passes
[ ] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [cap: cap-binary-runs] Ensure helpers-native binary is copied to project root after successful build; verify cap-binary-runs gate passes with MCP schemas check
[ ] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [cap: cap-mcp-answers] Verify cap-mcp-answers MCP integration is working end-to-end; gate currently passing with schema response
[ ] [scout] [ask: charter-bin] [defaults] Fix stale command references in AGENTS.md and claude-config/skills/ (grep shows 'helpers grade', 'cs_lint', 'strict_lint' still referenced but removed from CLI)
::end

::heading level=2 id=findings
Findings
::end

::paragraph id=findings-notes
A ledger of open defects and sharp edges. A claim that can be checked mechanically is written as a `::code run` block that checks it, declaring the files it judges with `reads=` — then the recorded verdict goes stale the moment the described code changes, and every read re-runs it, so this ledger cannot lie the way a hand-kept list does. A check that must build or test the project grants its build directory with `writes=` (for example `writes=target`). Prose bullets are only for what no check can hold: what breaks, where, what was tried. Delete findings when fixed.
::end

::bulleted-list id=bulleted-list-9
- **Stale command references** (found during the 2026-08-14 dx migration): `AGENTS.md` and the Claude `helpers` skill (`claude-config/skills/`) still reference `helpers grade`, `cs_lint`, and `strict_lint` as if they were live commands/tools. They verified as gone against `native/src/cli.rs`/`mcp.rs` — `README.md`'s tool list was already correct. Not yet fixed; needs a follow-up pass.
- **`dev.dx` gates scaffolded but not yet run/approved**: `cargo test --offline --locked` (whole native/ suite — expect several minutes, this crate has long-running integration tests per `native/usage.dx`), `cargo clippy`, `cargo fmt --check`. Run `dx run dev.dx` with `approve=true` to record the first green when convenient.
::end

::heading level=2 id=recipes
How a change flows
::end

::paragraph id=recipes-note
TODO: recipes — for each common kind of change (a new flag, a new module, a fix), the ordered list of files it touches. Write the first recipe the moment your first change lands; recipes are what make the second change cheap.
::end

::heading level=2 id=verification
Verification — what green means
::end

::paragraph id=verification-note
`dx run dev.dx` runs the gates — scaffolded from the cargo project — inside the sandbox and records each verdict in the document; a verdict goes stale exactly when the files its gate reads change. The recorded verdicts are the proof of done. First run: review the gates, then `dx run dev.dx --approve`.
::end

::heading level=2 id=trace
Traced index
::end

::paragraph id=trace-note
`dx trace --brief` maps the tree into a real symbol + reference index — named functions, structs, classes, and the files that reference each one — ranked by fan-in, not the file-stem heuristic the areas below use. This run block re-derives it whenever a file under its `reads=` tree changes; review it, then approve like any other gate (`dx run index.dx --approve`).
::end

::code id=index-trace lang=bash run reads=agent-config,atlas-api,bin,claude-config,community-cache,copilot-config,corpus,crawl-index,extraDocs,knowledge,lib,lint-checkers,lint-index,lint-modules,man,native,pages,proposals,release-notes,research-sources,scripts,templates,vscode-extension timeout=900
dx trace --brief .
::end

