::paragraph id=area-native-notes
The Rust crate building "the AI we are building" — a linter whose rules are *learned* from a language's own documentation rather than hand-written. **Extensive**: full docs live in `native/index.dx`, which links to `laws.dx` (permanent owner-ruled design laws), `architecture.dx` (current built system), `history.dx` (PASS-by-PASS development history, PASS 8–41+), `paper.dx` (the system paper), and `usage.dx` (how an agent uses the linter day to day). Migrated from the former root `LINTER.md` (7010 lines), `PAPER.md`, and `LINT_AGENTS.md` — all three deleted, dx is now the sole source of truth, and ~295 in-source comment references across native/src, native/tests, native/examples were updated to point at the new docs.
::end

